- D4-4 the wall clock is the draft's truth: instants always derive from (wall clock, zone); changing only the zone of a timed Event therefore sends `timezone`, `startAt` and `endAt` and moves the instants; unchanged wall-clock fields never put a time key in a PATCH. Pinned by the zone-change cases, by the three Events stored in the repeated hour or after the gap (a title-only edit sends only the title), and by the end-only edit of an Event that starts in the repeated hour.
- The PATCH keys of Task 1 item 9: a start move (day, time or zone) sends BOTH `startAt` and `endAt`; an end-only move sends `endAt` alone; toggling *Dia inteiro* sends `allDay` plus ONLY the target shape's keys; an all-day start-day move sends both days, a last-day move `endDate` alone, a zone-only change `timezone` alone; `{}` when nothing changed AND when the draft has an error.
- D4-8 the end does not follow the start: a start moved past the end that stays is an error (`{}` patch), not a shifted end.
- D4-10 a partly typed end is completed from the start (a missing day takes the start day, a missing time takes the start time, a fully empty end takes start plus one hour), always shown before saving (`draftEndPreview`).
- Task 1 item 7 (the one resolution rule) and its consequences: a wall clock inside the spring-forward gap is read with the offset before it, so a New York start at 02:30 with an end at 03:00 is `end_before_start` (07:30 UTC against 07:00 UTC) while an end at 03:30 is accepted (equal instants); a repeated hour resolves to its first occurrence on both sides of the comparison; an all-day event toggled to timed starts at the kept 09:00 and ends at its last day plus the start's clock time; the same wall-clock draft is refused in New York across the gap and accepted in São Paulo.
- Task 1 item 10: the preview is `{ day, time }` from the resolved end instant through `instantToWallClock`, so a one-hour default across the gap previews `03:30` (not `02:30`) and a typed end inside the gap previews the wall clock it resolves to; `null` exactly when the start cannot be resolved or the end is fully given; an all-day preview is `{ day: <first day or inclusive last day>, time: null }`.
- Task 1 item 5: a zone `isValidTimeZone` refuses falls back to America/Sao_Paulo, and the draft's wall-clock parts are then read in that fallback zone (the interface defines every part as the wall clock "in `timezone`"); only the day parts of an all-day DTO that lacks its days are pinned empty, all four parts of a timed DTO that lacks its start.
- Task 1 item 11: `timeZoneChoices` is the owner's zone first, then the current zone when it differs and is valid (so `UTC`, which V8 omits from `Intl.supportedValuesOf`, still appears), then every entry of `supported` not already present in the given order - read to include duplicates inside `supported` - as a fresh array, never mutating its input.
- Task 2: D4-2 the sheet keeps a snapshot of the Event (the open target carries it; edits and no-ops leave it unchanged); one draft per commitment id and one per DAY for new ones (`new:<day>`); a Google row returns the very same state object; an unknown zone is dropped from an `edit`; `request-delete` only for an edit target in the form view and `cancel-delete` only from the confirmation; `close` keeps every draft; `saved` and `deleted` drop the draft of their own key with a fresh `drafts` object and close the sheet only when that key is the open one; every no-op the plan names returns the very same state object (AC-A5).
- Task 3: the 404 mapping with `staleList: true`, every other cause through the generic classifier with `staleList: false`, the server's text never shown, a non-numeric `status` is not a 404; `eventsSearchPath` is `/api/events?q=` plus `encodeURIComponent(q.trim())` with no range and no minimum length; the search label is `dd/MM/aaaa · HH:mm` in the OWNER's zone (plan decision D3-1, the New York Event at 14:00 UTC reads 11:00) and `dd/MM/aaaa · dia todo` with the first day verbatim; `decideSearchBody` is evaluated in the plan's order (offline, hint, task-error, loading, results, commitments failed -> results, commitments unanswered -> loading, empty), so a Task failure outranks anything the commitments found and an unanswered Task search outranks commitments already found.
